🚀 Day 4 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 1552 – Magnetic Force Between Two Balls.

This problem strengthened my understanding of Binary Search on the Answer and how a greedy placement strategy can be used to maximize the minimum distance between placed balls.

💡 Approach: Binary Search + Greedy Placement (O(n log(maxDistance)))

First, I sorted the basket positions. Then, I applied Binary Search on the possible answer (minimum magnetic force). For every candidate distance, I used a Greedy approach to place the balls while maintaining at least that minimum distance. If placing all m balls was possible, I searched for a larger distance; otherwise, I reduced the search space. This efficiently found the maximum possible minimum distance.

📚 Key Learnings:
✅ Mastering the Binary Search on Answer technique
✅ Applying a Greedy strategy for optimal placement
✅ Understanding optimization problems with sorted arrays
✅ Reducing the search space efficiently instead of brute force
✅ Achieving an optimized O(n log(maxDistance)) solution

